@Darren The clue didn't say what kind of suspicious -- and it definitely didn't say the *sender* was suspicious.  Late-week clues are often misdirects on purpose.

If you haven't seen a mangosteen, do an internet search.  They look just as the clue describes them.

As to the "perhaps", I've seen comments along the lines of "The clue says A and the answer says B but not all As are Bs".  Adding a "perhaps" makes this explicit.  e.g. not all suspicious links have NSFW content, but some do, when the suspicious aspect of the link makes it look suspiciously NSFW.  It can even be a clue that the first association you have (e.g. suspicious meaning spam or scam) isn't necessarily the right one...
